Z||000017||yo_sweets_babe||08-25-2001||12:11 AM||||aight, one word - FATE<BR>nothing can be blamed for earnhardt's death - not bill simpson, dale's pit crew, nascar, ken schrader, or a seat belt - it was just a fact of life.<BR>a black box would be pointless - it would alwayz be messed up from force, heat, static, etc etc.  besides, no one's gonna hear much from it after when the car slams into a concrete wall or another car.<BR>and my biggest peeve - why is it such a big deal when a driver is killed?  these people take their lives into their own hands and speed around a concrete track at 200mph, meanwhile dodging other cars who are doing the same thing - crashes are expected.  these people know the risks, and they follow them - plus they follow their heart and their dreams.  they die doing something they love.  don't bother investigating into their deaths, it was expected, so let them be.||||reg||1
Z||000018||ray b||08-25-2001||10:42 PM||||and how would you know if your street car had a black box sliped into it at the factory or the dealer? i heard some do right now and you will only be told of the black box after itis tooo late. real world axident date is the cover story they use now.<BR>hear about the car rential co and gps speeding fines in N E story.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
